W4/W6 — BLE-over-air diagnosis (after the W6 shared-bus-lock fix)   2026-06-20
=============================================================================
Board: rpi_pico2/rp2350a/m33/w   Debug Probe if01 + host BlueZ/bleak
Builds: build_whd (BT_SHELL, manual) and build_whd_soak (auto BLE peripheral),
        both CONFIG_CYW43_TRANSPORT_WHD=y + the W6 shared bus lock.

FINDINGS (BLE advertising/connection over WHD coex)
---------------------------------------------------
1. Advertising DOES work and IS emitted over-air. BT_SHELL build, manual
   `bt init` (BD_ADDR 88:A2:9E:D1:6D:A0 verified) + `bt advertise on`
   ("Advertising started") -> host BleakScanner FINDS test-picow-bluetooth.
   So the HCI adv-setup commands complete and the controller radiates. The
   earlier soak "not discoverable" was NOT a dead adv path.
2. BUT the link is MARGINAL and ERRATIC:
   - RSSI ~ -92 dBm when seen (abnormally weak for a bench device; expect
     -40..-60). Sometimes not discovered at all within a 7-12 s scan window.
   - ble_central.py finds + connects, then "EARLY DISCONNECT (unexpected):
     failed to discover services, device disconnected" — the link drops during
     GATT service discovery (the first burst of ATT request/response ACL
     round-trips).
3. Net effect on the coex soak: ble_central.py gets 0 stable connections /
   0 notifications (build_whd_soak, 3+4 cycles), even though device-side coex is
   healthy (WiFi associates with BT active, 0 faults — the W6 lock fix holds).

LIKELY CAUSES (for the next iteration)
--------------------------------------
A. BT RX latency/starvation. RX is a 4 ms TIMER poll (whd_bt_glue.c
   bt_poll_thread) with NO host-wake IRQ hook. Worse, the W6 shared bus lock
   makes the BT poll BLOCK whenever WHD's WLAN thread holds the bus, so RX
   latency spikes under WiFi activity. Sustained ACL (service discovery,
   notifications) needs prompt, low-jitter RX — the poll likely can't keep the
   connection's ATT round-trips inside timing, causing the early disconnect.
   => Real fix: host-wake-IRQ-driven BT RX (not a fixed poll), and/or BT-first
      arbitration so BT RX is serviced ahead of WLAN (mirrors the georgerobotics
      single-poll BT-first design, REFERENCE §2.3). Note WHD OWNS the shared
      host-wake IRQ on GP24 (airoc_whd_hal_spi.c whd_bus_spi_irq_*), so BT must
      hook/share it rather than add a second IRQ.
B. Weak RSSI (-92). Possibly BT TX power / WiFi+BT coex arbitration not
   configured the way the georgerobotics cyw43_ll path did (same antenna + BT
   firmware gave strong, stable links + 6073 notif in the georgerobotics soak).
   Investigate coex/Tx-power config the georgerobotics stack applies that WHD
   bring-up does not.

STATUS: device-side §2.7 coex contention = FIXED (W6 part 1). BLE link
robustness over WHD = NOT yet achieved -> W4 (notification baseline) and W6 (2 h
gate) remain IN-PROGRESS, blocked here. No fabricated pass.
